  "question": "求极限 $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{1}{\\ln n}\\sum_{k = 1}^{n}\\frac{1}{k}.$",
  "answer": "$\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{1}{\\ln n}\\sum_{k = 1}^{n}\\frac{1}{k} = 1.$",
  "ref_source": "textbook:puheping_math_contest_v2",
  "techniques": [
    "施笃兹定理",
    "极限计算"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "text": "分析 分母是 $\\ln n$ ，分子最好能用对应的函数形式来估计。由于 $(\\ln x)'|_{x=k} = \\frac{1}{k}$ ，所以想到用定积分的不等式性质来对分子做放大与缩小。"
      },
      {
        "id": "s2",
        "text": "由于 $y = \\frac{1}{x}$ 在 $x > 0$ 时单调递减，则"
      },
      {
        "id": "s3",
        "text": "\\int_ {k} ^ {k + 1} \\frac {1}{x} \\mathrm{d} x \\leqslant \\frac {1}{k} \\leqslant \\int_ {k - 1} ^ {k} \\frac {1}{x} \\mathrm{d} x,"
      },
      {
        "id": "s4",
        "text": "\\int_ {1} ^ {n + 1} \\frac {1}{x} d x = \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\int_ {k} ^ {k + 1} \\frac {1}{x} d x \\leqslant \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\frac {1}{k} \\leqslant \\sum_ {k = 2} ^ {n} \\int_ {k - 1} ^ {k} \\frac {1}{x} d x + 1 = \\int_ {1} ^ {n} \\frac {1}{x} d x + 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "s5",
        "text": "即"
      },
      {
        "id": "s6",
        "text": "\\ln (n + 1) \\leqslant \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\frac {1}{k} \\leqslant \\ln n + 1 \\Rightarrow \\frac {\\ln (n + 1)}{\\ln n} \\leqslant \\frac {1}{\\ln n} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {n} \\frac {1}{k} \\leqslant \\frac {\\ln n + 1}{\\ln n}."
      },
      {
        "id": "s7",
        "text": "由于 $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{\\ln(n + 1)}{\\ln n} = 1 = \\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{\\ln n + 1}{\\ln n}$ ，所以 $\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{1}{\\ln n}\\sum_{k = 1}^{n}\\frac{1}{k} = 1.$"
      }
    ],
    "final_answer": "$\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{1}{\\ln n}\\sum_{k = 1}^{n}\\frac{1}{k} = 1.$",
    "techniques_used": [
      "施笃兹定理",
      "极限计算"
    ]
  },
